{"id": "SGU_Episode_662", "title": "SGU Episode 662", "type": "structured", "description": "The Skeptic's Guide to the Universe, Episode 662 Transcript", "metadata": {"title": "SGU Episode 662", "date": "March 17 2024", "year": 2024, "month": 3, "day": 17, "rogues": ["Steven Novella", "Jay Novella", "Evan Bernstein", "Bob Novella", "Cara Santa Maria"], "quotee_url": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephen_Hawking", "quote": "\n Remember to look up at the stars and not down at your feet. Try to make sense of what you see and wonder about what makes the universe exist. And however difficult life may seem, there is always something you can do and succeed at. It matters that you don't just give up. \n", "quotee": "\n Stephen Hawking ", "quotee_title": "  English theoretical physicist\n", "categories": [], "podcast_url": "https://www.theskepticsguide.org/podcasts/episode-662", "episode_number": 662}, "sections": [{"id": 0, "text": "Voice-over: You're listening to the Skeptics' Guide to the Universe, your escape to reality.\n", "title": "Introduction, Pi Day", "metadata": {"title": "Introduction, Pi Day"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 1, "text": "Stephen Hawking: Visionary physicist dies aged 76[1]", "title": "In Memoriam: Stephen Hawking", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:00:52", "hour": 0, "minute": "0", "second": "52", "links": ["https://www.bbc.com/news/uk-43396008"], "title": "In Memoriam: Stephen Hawking"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 2, "text": "Brenda Milner, British-Canadian neuropsychologist", "title": "Forgotten Superheroes of Science", "metadata": {"timestamp": "0:15:11", "hour": 0, "minute": "15", "second": "11", "title": "Forgotten Superheroes of Science"}, "sections": []}, {"id": 3, "text": "", "title": "News Items", "metadata": {"title": "News Items"}, "sections": [{"id": 4, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "S", "speaker": "Steven Novella"}}, {"id": 5, "text": "", "metadata": {"speaker_abbreviation": "B", "speaker": "Bob Novella"}}, {"id": 6, "text": "", 